    explanation: 'NO CHANGE is correct because "Based on this data" is a standard, correctly formed introductory participial phrase, and the sentence is already clear and appropriately concise. The second option adds the redundant tag "either," which repeats the negation already established by "not just," adding no new meaning. "Basing it on this data" awkwardly and unnecessarily adds the pronoun "it," which has no clear antecedent and disrupts the sentence\'s flow. "Based off of" is a nonstandard variant of the idiom; standard written English uses "based on," not "based off of." ACT Tip: Watch for nonstandard idiomatic phrases like "based off of" — standard written English requires "based on."',
