    explanation: 'NO CHANGE is correct because the phrase "along with two apprentices" is a parenthetical modifier, not part of the grammatical subject, so the verb must agree with the singular subject "Ostrowski": "spent" is correct past-tense singular agreement. "Spend" is present tense and does not agree in tense with the rest of the passage\'s past-tense narration, nor in number with a singular subject. "Have spent" incorrectly treats the parenthetical phrase as making the subject plural. "Spending" removes the finite verb and creates a fragment. ACT Tip: Phrases like "along with," "as well as," and "together with" do not make a subject plural — the verb still agrees with the original singular subject.',
