    questionText: 'According to the passage, the pilot program provided selected residents with:',
    options: [
      'a monthly payment of five hundred dollars for two years',
      'a one-time payment of five hundred dollars',
      'job training vouchers worth five hundred dollars per month',
      'a monthly payment that increased each year to match inflation',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'A',
    explanation: 'The passage states the program provided "a guaranteed monthly payment of five hundred dollars" for a period of "two years." A one-time payment misreads the recurring monthly structure described in the passage. Job training vouchers are never mentioned as the form the payment took; the passage specifies the payment was unconditional cash. The passage explicitly notes the payment amount was fixed and did not include an inflation adjustment, which several researchers later recommended precisely because it had been absent, contradicting the fourth option. ACT Tip: For questions about a program\'s basic structure, locate the specific sentence describing amount, frequency, and duration rather than relying on later details about related but distinct issues, like inflation.',
