deo consultations, while imperfect, have allowed patients to receive care they would have otherwise gone without entirely[13]. [14]Some skeptics worry that telemedicine could eventually replace in-person care too broadly, reducing the quality of the doctor-patient relationship[14]. [15]Vasquez responds that the program was never intended to replace in-person visits, only to fill gaps that distance had long left unfilled[15].',
    questionText: '[underlined: Psychiatric consultations, in particular, have grown rapidly, reflecting a broader shortage of mental health providers across rural America]',
    options: [
