ing lane[12]. [13]The city ultimately redesigned that single intersection twice more before settling on a configuration that satisfied both cyclists and drivers[13]. [14]Reyes describes this ongoing troubleshooting as an unavoidable part of any major infrastructure project, no design works perfectly the first time[14]. [15]He hopes Halbrook\'s experience, successes and setbacks alike, will offer useful lessons for other mid-sized cities considering similar projects[15].',
    questionText: '[underlined: Other business owners, particularly those near university housing, supported the change immediately]',
