      'Other business owners particularly those near university housing supported the change immediately',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'A',
    explanation: 'NO CHANGE is correct because the parenthetical phrase "particularly those near university housing" is properly set off by a comma on both sides, correctly marking it as additional, nonessential information interrupting the main clause. Removing the second comma, as in the second option, leaves the parenthetical improperly set off on only one side. Removing the first comma, as in the third option, leaves the same problem on the other side. Removing both commas, as in the fourth option, fails to set off the parenthetical at all, making the sentence harder to parse correctly. ACT Tip: A parenthetical phrase interrupting a sentence\'s subject and verb requires a comma on both sides, not just one or none.',
