      'Ferrer began documenting his techniques on video several years ago, creating an archive intended to outlast any single workshop or teacher',
      'To address this concern, Ferrer began documenting his techniques on video several years ago',
      'To address this concern, which was a real concern for him, Ferrer began documenting his techniques on video several years ago, creating an archive intended to outlast any single workshop or teacher',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'A',
    explanation: 'NO CHANGE is correct because the sentence connects Ferrer\'s specific concern about disappearing techniques directly to his specific response, video documentation, and explains the archive\'s purpose, outlasting any single workshop or teacher, which supports the following sentences about the video collection. Removing "To address this concern," as in the second option, loses the direct causal link between the previous paragraph\'s concern and this response. Removing "creating an archive intended to outlast any single workshop or teacher," as in the third option, cuts the explanation of the archive\'s broader purpose, weakening the connection to the passage\'s closing themes about preservation. The fourth option adds the vague, redundant phrase "which was a real concern for him," restating something the sentence already conveys through "this concern." ACT Tip: When a sentence directly responds to a concern or problem raised in the previous sentence, preserving that causal connection, along with the explanation of the response\'s purpose, usually strengthens the passage\'s logical flow.',
