    questionText: 'Which of the following best characterizes the overall relationship between the passage\'s discussion of decision fatigue research across different settings, such as courtrooms and consumer shopping?',
    options: [
      'Every study across every setting has found strong, consistent, easily replicable evidence for decision fatigue',
      'The evidence is mixed: some studies broadly support the theory while others have struggled to replicate the effect under tightly controlled conditions, leaving open questions about its robustness and generalizability',
      'No study in any setting has ever found any evidence at all supporting decision fatigue',
      'The theory has been abandoned entirely by researchers in favor of unrelated explanations',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'B',
    explanation: 'The passage explicitly describes "notably mixed results," citing consumer studies broadly consistent with the theory alongside other researchers who "have struggled to replicate decision fatigue effects under more tightly controlled laboratory conditions," directly supporting this characterization of mixed, unresolved evidence. The passage explicitly describes struggles to replicate the effect in some studies, directly contradicting a claim of universally strong, consistent evidence. The passage describes some studies finding results broadly consistent with the theory, directly contradicting a claim that no study has ever found supporting evidence. The passage states most researchers continue to accept some version of decision fatigue as real, directly contradicting a claim that the theory has been entirely abandoned. ACT Tip: When a passage explicitly uses language like "mixed results" to summarize a body of research, expect the correct answer to reflect that acknowledged uncertainty rather than an overstated claim in either direction.',
