    questionText: 'Which of the following variables was held constant across all conditions in Experiments 1 and 2, based on the passage?',
    options: [
      'Fertilizer type',
      'Duration of sunlight exposure per day',
      'Number of flower buds per plant',
      'Plant height at 30 days',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'B',
    explanation: 'The passage states that "all plants receiving the same amount of water, sunlight (14 hours per day), and starting soil composition," directly identifying sunlight duration as a controlled, unvarying factor. Fertilizer type is precisely the variable being deliberately varied across conditions in Experiments 1 and 2, not held constant. The number of flower buds per plant is a measured outcome in Experiment 2, not a controlled input variable the researchers held constant. Plant height at 30 days is similarly a measured outcome, not something the researchers held constant. ACT Tip: Distinguish clearly between variables the researchers deliberately varied to test their effects and variables they held constant to isolate those effects; only the constants should be selected when asked what was "held constant."',
