      'He acknowledges that not every library system has the technical staff capacity to handle a similar transition successfully',
      'He acknowledges that not every library system has the technical staff capacity to manipulate a similar transition successfully',
      'He acknowledges that not every library system has the technical staff capacity to operate a similar transition successfully',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'A',
    explanation: 'NO CHANGE is correct because "manage" is the standard, precise word for overseeing and successfully carrying out a complex organizational process like a software transition. "Handle" is a plausible near-synonym but is somewhat more informal and general, a slightly less precise fit for describing a large-scale, structured organizational undertaking. "Manipulate" carries a negative connotation of controlling something deceptively or improperly, an inappropriate and inaccurate fit for describing a legitimate, transparent organizational transition. "Operate" is typically used for running an ongoing system or piece of equipment, rather than overseeing a discrete, one-time organizational transition process. ACT Tip: When a word choice question involves overseeing a process or project, consider whether the near-synonym implies legitimate, structured management or carries an unrelated or negative connotation that does not fit the context.',
