]. [12]Smaller library systems, in particular, may lack the in-house expertise that made Brightwater\'s transition ultimately manageable despite its early difficulties[12]. [13]Delacroix has begun consulting informally with several neighboring library directors considering similar transitions[13]. [14]He is careful to emphasize that open-source software is not automatically the right choice for every library, only that it worked well for Brightwater\'s particular circumstances[14]. [15]Whether other library systems follow Brightwater\'s example will likely depend as much on available technical staffing as on the software\'s underlying cost advantages[15].',
