      'This erosion reduction has proven particularly valuable during recent hurricane seasons, when the restored mangroves appear to have measurably shrunk storm surge damage to nearby coastal properties',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'A',
    explanation: 'NO CHANGE is correct because "reduced" is the most natural, precise word for describing a measured decrease in storm damage, matching the passage\'s clear, accessible tone throughout. "Lessened" is a plausible near-synonym but is somewhat more literary and slightly less common in this specific technical, measurement-based context. "Diminished" is also plausible but carries a slightly more formal connotation, a less natural fit than "reduced" for describing a measured statistical decrease. "Shrunk" typically describes a physical object becoming smaller in size, an imprecise and unusual fit for describing a decrease in the amount or severity of storm damage. ACT Tip: When multiple near-synonyms could technically fit a sentence, favor the one most naturally and commonly paired with the specific type of measured, quantifiable change being described.',
  ),
