    correctAnswer: 'A',
    explanation: 'NO CHANGE is correct because the singular subject "variation" correctly takes the singular verb "has," and no commas are needed within this correctly structured sentence, since "applicable to every swimmer regardless of body type" is an essential modifying phrase describing the specific template being discussed. "Have," in the second option, incorrectly uses a plural verb form for the singular subject "variation." Adding a comma before "applicable to every swimmer," as in the third option, incorrectly separates this essential modifying phrase from the noun it describes. Adding a comma after "efforts," as in the fourth option, incorrectly separates the noun from the essential infinitive phrase completing its meaning. ACT Tip: Do not insert a comma before an essential modifying phrase that specifies exactly which version of a noun, such as which "template," is being discussed.',
