    explanation: 'The slope formula is m = (y2 - y1) / (x2 - x1) = (14 - 2) / (7 - 3) = 12 / 4 = 3. ACT Tip: Keep the order of subtraction consistent between x-coordinates and y-coordinates when applying the slope formula.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-geo-015',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Geometry',
    difficulty: Difficulty.easy,
    questionText: 'A circle has a radius of 9 meters. What is its circumference, in meters, in terms of pi?',
    options: [
      '9 pi',
      '18 pi',
      '27 pi',
      '81 pi',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'B',
    explanation: 'Circumference is given by C = 2 x pi x r = 2 x pi x 9 = 18 pi meters. ACT Tip: Distinguish the circumference formula, 2 pi r, from the area formula, pi r^2, since confusing them is a common error.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-spd-016',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Statistics and Probability',
    difficulty: Difficulty.easy,
    questionText: 'What is the median of the data set 11, 4, 17, 8, 22, 6?',
    options: [
      '8',
      '9.5',
      '11',
      '12.5',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'B',
    explanation: 'Arrange the data in order: 4, 6, 8, 11, 17, 22. With six values, the median is the average of the two middle values, 8 and 11: (8 + 11) / 2 = 19 / 2 = 9.5. ACT Tip: With an even number of data points, the median is the average of the two middle values, not either value alone.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-alg-017',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Algebra',
    difficulty: Difficulty.easy,
    questionText: 'If 4x + y = 23 and y = 7, what is the value of x?',
    options: [
      '3',
      '4',
      '5',
      '6',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'B',
    explanation: 'Substitute y = 7 into the first equation: 4x + 7 = 23. Subtract 7 from both sides: 4x = 16. Divide by 4: x = 4. Checking, 4(4) + 7 = 16 + 7 = 23, which matches. ACT Tip: When one variable already has a numeric value, substitute it immediately to reduce the system to a single-variable equation.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-num-018',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Number and Quantity',
    difficulty: Difficulty.easy,
    questionText: 'What is the value of 7.2 x 10^3 written as a standard number?',
    options: [
      '72',
      '720',
      '7200',
      '72000',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'C',
    explanation: 'Multiplying by 10^3 moves the decimal point three places to the right: 7.2 becomes 7200. ACT Tip: When converting from scientific notation, move the decimal point right for a positive exponent by exactly the number of places the exponent indicates.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-geo-019',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Geometry',
    difficulty: Difficulty.easy,
    questionText: 'A right triangle has legs of length 5 and 12. What is the length of its hypotenuse?',
    options: [
      '13',
      '15',
      '17',
      '19',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'A',
    explanation: 'By the Pythagorean theorem, c^2 = a^2 + b^2 = 5^2 + 12^2 = 25 + 144 = 169. Taking the square root, c = 13. ACT Tip: Recognize common right triangle ratios like 5-12-13 and 3-4-5, which can save time on Pythagorean theorem problems.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-fun-020',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Functions',
    difficulty: Difficulty.easy,
    questionText: 'If g(x) = 5x - 6, for what value of x does g(x) = 19?',
    options: [
      '4',
      '5',
      '6',
      '25',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'B',
    explanation: 'Set the function equal to 19: 5x - 6 = 19. Add 6 to both sides: 5x = 25. Divide by 5: x = 5. Checking, g(5) = 5(5) - 6 = 25 - 6 = 19, which matches. ACT Tip: To find an input value given an output, set the function expression equal to that output and solve like any other equation.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-alg-021',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Algebra',
    difficulty: Difficulty.medium,
    questionText: 'Solve the system of equations: 4x + y = 22 and x - y = 3.',
    options: [
      'x = 4, y = 6',
      'x = 5, y = 2',
      'x = 6, y = -2',
      'x = 3, y = 10',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'B',
    explanation: 'Add the two equations to eliminate y: (4x + y) + (x - y) = 22 + 3, giving 5x = 25, so x = 5. Substitute into x - y = 3: 5 - y = 3, so y = 2. Checking in the first equation, 4(5) + 2 = 20 + 2 = 22, which matches. ACT Tip: When two equations contain opposite-sign coefficients for the same variable, adding them directly eliminates that variable.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-fun-022',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Functions',
    difficulty: Difficulty.medium,
    questionText: 'If f(x) = x^2 - 2x + 6, what is f(5)?',
    options: [
      '21',
      '23',
      '25',
      '27',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'A',
    explanation: 'Substitute x = 5: f(5) = (5)^2 - 2(5) + 6 = 25 - 10 + 6 = 21. ACT Tip: Substitute the input value into every instance of x before performing any arithmetic, to avoid missing a term.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-geo-023',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Geometry',
    difficulty: Difficulty.medium,
    questionText: 'A cylinder has a radius of 5 cm and a height of 8 cm. What is its volume, in cubic centimeters, in terms of pi?',
    options: [
      '40 pi',
      '80 pi',
      '160 pi',
      '200 pi',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'D',
    explanation: 'The volume of a cylinder is V = pi r^2 h = pi (5)^2 (8) = pi (25)(8) = 200 pi cubic centimeters. ACT Tip: Square only the radius, not the height, in the cylinder volume formula.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-spd-024',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Statistics and Probability',
    difficulty: Difficulty.medium,
    questionText: 'A jar contains 6 blue candies, 8 green candies, and 4 red candies. If two candies are drawn without replacement, what is the probability that both are blue?',
    options: [
      '5/51',
      '1/9',
      '5/153',
      '6/18',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'A',
    explanation: 'There are 18 candies total. The probability the first candy is blue is 6/18, which simplifies to 1/3. Without replacement, 5 blue candies remain out of 17 total, so the probability the second is also blue is 5/17. Multiply: (1/3)(5/17) = 5/51. ACT Tip: For without-replacement probability, multiply the probability of the first event by the updated probability of the second event based on the reduced total, simplifying each fraction as you go.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-num-025',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Number and Quantity',
    difficulty: Difficulty.medium,
    questionText: 'Simplify: (4x^3 y^2) x (2x y^5).',
    options: [
      '8x^4 y^7',
      '8x^3 y^10',
      '6x^4 y^7',
      '8x^4 y^10',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'A',
    explanation: 'Multiply the coefficients: 4 x 2 = 8. Add the exponents of matching variables: x^3 x x^1 = x^(3+1) = x^4, and y^2 x y^5 = y^(2+5) = y^7. The result is 8x^4 y^7. ACT Tip: When multiplying exponential terms with the same base, add the exponents; never multiply them.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-alg-026',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Algebra',
    difficulty: Difficulty.medium,
    questionText: 'Factor the expression: x^2 + 11x + 24.',
    options: [
      '(x + 3)(x + 8)',
      '(x + 4)(x + 6)',
      '(x + 2)(x + 12)',
      '(x - 3)(x - 8)',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'A',
    explanation: 'Find two numbers that multiply to 24 and add to 11: 3 and 8 satisfy both conditions (3 x 8 = 24, 3 + 8 = 11). The expression factors as (x + 3)(x + 8). Checking by expanding: x^2 + 8x + 3x + 24 = x^2 + 11x + 24, which matches. ACT Tip: To factor a trinomial with a leading coefficient of 1, find two numbers whose product is the constant term and whose sum is the middle coefficient.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-fun-027',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Functions',
    difficulty: Difficulty.medium,
    questionText: 'The function h(t) = -16t^2 + 80t models the height, in feet, of a ball t seconds after being thrown. At what time does the ball reach its maximum height?',
    options: [
      '1.5 seconds',
      '2 seconds',
      '2.5 seconds',
      '3 seconds',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'C',
    explanation: 'For a quadratic h(t) = at^2 + bt, the vertex occurs at t = -b / (2a). Here a = -16 and b = 80, so t = -80 / (2 x -16) = -80 / -32 = 2.5 seconds. ACT Tip: For any quadratic in the form at^2 + bt + c, the vertex\'s t-coordinate is always -b / (2a).',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-geo-028',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Geometry',
    difficulty: Difficulty.medium,
    questionText: 'A rectangular prism has a length of 7 in, width of 4 in, and height of 5 in. What is its surface area, in square inches?',
    options: [
      '146',
      '156',
      '166',
      '176',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'C',
    explanation: 'Surface area of a rectangular prism is SA = 2(lw + lh + wh) = 2((7)(4) + (7)(5) + (4)(5)) = 2(28 + 35 + 20) = 2(83) = 166 square inches. ACT Tip: Compute each of the three distinct face-pair areas separately before doubling the sum, to avoid missing one of the three pairs of faces.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-spd-029',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Statistics and Probability',
    difficulty: Difficulty.medium,
    questionText: 'A data set has a mean of 28 and consists of 7 values. If one value of 21 is removed, what is the new mean of the remaining 6 values?',
    options: [
      '28.83',
      '29.17',
      '29.5',
      '30',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'B',
    explanation: 'The original sum of all 7 values is 28 x 7 = 196. Removing the value 21 leaves a sum of 196 - 21 = 175 across 6 values. The new mean is 175 / 6, which is approximately 29.17 when rounded to two decimal places. ACT Tip: Recover the original total sum by multiplying the mean by the original count, then subtract the removed value before dividing by the new count.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-num-030',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Number and Quantity',
    difficulty: Difficulty.medium,
    questionText: 'What is the value of the expression (5/6) + (1/4) - (2/3)? Express your answer as a fraction in simplest form.',
    options: [
      '1/4',
      '1/3',
      '5/12',
      '7/12',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'C',
    explanation: 'Find a common denominator for 6, 4, and 3, which is 12. Convert each fraction: 5/6 = 10/12, 1/4 = 3/12, and 2/3 = 8/12. Compute 10/12 + 3/12 - 8/12 = 5/12. This fraction is already in simplest form, since 5 and 12 share no common factors other than 1. ACT Tip: When adding or subtracting fractions with different denominators, convert to a common denominator before combining numerators, then check whether the result can be simplified further.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-alg-031',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Algebra',
    difficulty: Difficulty.medium,
    questionText: 'If 5(x - 2) = 3(x + 6), what is the value of x?',
    options: [
      '12',
      '14',
      '16',
      '18',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'B',
    explanation: 'Distribute both sides: 5x - 10 = 3x + 18. Subtract 3x from both sides: 2x - 10 = 18. Add 10 to both sides: 2x = 28. Divide by 2: x = 14. Checking, 5(14 - 2) = 5(12) = 60, and 3(14 + 6) = 3(20) = 60, which matches. ACT Tip: Distribute fully on both sides of an equation before attempting to isolate the variable.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-fun-032',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Functions',
    difficulty: Difficulty.medium,
    questionText: 'If f(x) = 4x + 1 and g(x) = x^2, what is f(g(3))?',
    options: [
      '13',
      '25',
      '37',
      '40',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'C',
    explanation: 'First evaluate g(3) = (3)^2 = 9. Then evaluate f(9) = 4(9) + 1 = 36 + 1 = 37. ACT Tip: For composite functions, evaluate the innermost function first, then use that result as the input for the outer function.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-geo-033',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Geometry',
    difficulty: Difficulty.medium,
    questionText: 'In a circle, a central angle measures 120 degrees and the radius is 12 cm. What is the length of the arc formed by this angle, in terms of pi?',
    options: [
      '4 pi',
      '8 pi',
      '12 pi',
      '16 pi',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'B',
    explanation: 'Arc length equals (central angle / 360) x circumference. The circumference is 2 x pi x 12 = 24 pi. The fraction of the circle is 120/360 = 1/3. Arc length = (1/3)(24 pi) = 8 pi cm. ACT Tip: Determine what fraction of the full circle the central angle represents, then apply that fraction to the total circumference.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-spd-034',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Statistics and Probability',
    difficulty: Difficulty.medium,
    questionText: 'A fair six-sided die is rolled twice. What is the probability that the sum of the two rolls is 7?',
    options: [
      '4/36',
      '5/36',
      '6/36',
      '7/36',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'C',
    explanation: 'There are 36 equally likely outcomes when rolling two dice. The combinations that sum to 7 are (1,6), (2,5), (3,4), (4,3), (5,2), and (6,1), a total of 6 outcomes. The probability is 6/36. ACT Tip: Systematically list every ordered pair that produces the target sum rather than trying to count them without writing them out.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-num-035',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Number and Quantity',
    difficulty: Difficulty.medium,
    questionText: 'A population of bacteria doubles every 4 hours. If there are initially 300 bacteria, how many bacteria are there after 16 hours?',
    options: [
      '2400',
      '3600',
      '4800',
      '6000',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'C',
    explanation: 'In 16 hours, the population doubles 16 / 4 = 4 times. Starting at 300, after four doublings: 300 x 2 x 2 x 2 x 2 = 300 x 16 = 4800 bacteria. ACT Tip: For repeated doubling problems, determine the number of doubling periods first, then multiply the starting value by 2 raised to that number of periods.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-alg-036',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Algebra',
    difficulty: Difficulty.medium,
    questionText: 'Solve for x: x^2 - 3x - 28 = 0.',
    options: [
      'x = 4 or x = -7',
      'x = 7 or x = -4',
      'x = 14 or x = -2',
      'x = 28 or x = -1',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'B',
    explanation: 'Find two numbers that multiply to -28 and add to -3: 7 and -4 satisfy both conditions, since 7 x -4 = -28 and 7 + -4 = 3, but checking the sign needed for sum -3: try -7 and 4: -7 x 4 = -28, -7 + 4 = -3, correct. The expression factors as (x - 7)(x + 4) = 0. Setting each factor to zero: x - 7 = 0 gives x = 7, and x + 4 = 0 gives x = -4. Checking: 7^2 - 3(7) - 28 = 49 - 21 - 28 = 0, and (-4)^2 - 3(-4) - 28 = 16 + 12 - 28 = 0, both correct. ACT Tip: For a quadratic with leading coefficient 1, find two numbers whose product is the constant term and whose sum is the coefficient of the middle term, keeping track of signs carefully.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-geo-037',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Geometry',
    difficulty: Difficulty.medium,
    questionText: 'Two similar triangles have a scale factor of 4:5. If the smaller triangle has an area of 32 square units, what is the area of the larger triangle?',
    options: [
      '40',
      '45',
      '50',
      '55',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'C',
    explanation: 'For similar figures, the ratio of areas equals the square of the ratio of corresponding sides: (4/5)^2 = 16/25. Set up the proportion 16/25 = 32/A, where A is the larger area. Cross-multiply: 16A = 25 x 32 = 800. Divide by 16: A = 50 square units. ACT Tip: The ratio of areas between similar figures is the square of the ratio of their corresponding side lengths, not the ratio itself.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-fun-038',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Functions',
    difficulty: Difficulty.medium,
    questionText: 'The graph of y = f(x) is shifted 4 units left and 3 units down to produce the graph of y = g(x). If f(x) = x^2, which of the following represents g(x)?',
    options: [
      'g(x) = (x - 4)^2 - 3',
      'g(x) = (x + 4)^2 - 3',
      'g(x) = (x - 4)^2 + 3',
      'g(x) = (x + 4)^2 + 3',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'B',
    explanation: 'A shift left by 4 units replaces x with (x + 4) inside the function, and a shift down by 3 units subtracts 3 from the entire function. Applying both transformations to f(x) = x^2 gives g(x) = (x + 4)^2 - 3. ACT Tip: Horizontal shifts work opposite to intuition; shifting left adds inside the parentheses with the input variable, while shifting right subtracts.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-spd-039',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Statistics and Probability',
    difficulty: Difficulty.medium,
    questionText: 'In a class of 28 students, 17 play video games, 13 read novels regularly, and 6 do both. How many students do neither?',
    options: [
      '2',
      '4',
      '6',
      '8',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'B',
    explanation: 'Using the inclusion-exclusion principle, the number of students who do at least one activity is 17 + 13 - 6 = 24. Subtracting from the total class size: 28 - 24 = 4 students do neither. ACT Tip: For overlapping group problems, subtract the "both" count once from the sum of the two individual groups to avoid double-counting before comparing to the total.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-num-040',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Number and Quantity',
    difficulty: Difficulty.medium,
    questionText: 'What is the greatest common factor of 72 and 108?',
    options: [
      '12',
      '18',
      '36',
      '72',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'C',
    explanation: 'Find the prime factorization of each number: 72 = 2^3 x 3^2, and 108 = 2^2 x 3^3. The greatest common factor takes the lowest power of each shared prime: 2^2 x 3^2 = 4 x 9 = 36. Checking, 72 / 36 = 2 and 108 / 36 = 3, both integers with no remaining common factor, confirming 36 is correct. ACT Tip: Use prime factorization to find a greatest common factor by multiplying only the shared primes at their lowest shared power.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-alg-041',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Algebra',
    difficulty: Difficulty.hard,
    questionText: 'If (x + 5)/(x - 2) = 7/3, what is the value of x?',
    options: [
      '29/4',
      '31/4',
      '27/4',
      '33/4',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'A',
    explanation: 'Cross-multiply: 3(x + 5) = 7(x - 2). Distribute: 3x + 15 = 7x - 14. Subtract 3x from both sides: 15 = 4x - 14. Add 14 to both sides: 29 = 4x. Divide by 4: x = 29/4. Checking, (29/4 + 5) / (29/4 - 2) = (49/4) / (21/4) = 49/21 = 7/3, which matches. ACT Tip: When solving a proportion with variables in the numerator and denominator, cross-multiply first, then distribute and isolate the variable.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-fun-042',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Functions',
    difficulty: Difficulty.hard,
    questionText: 'If f(x) = 4x - 3 and f(g(x)) = 8x + 5, what is g(x)?',
    options: [
      'g(x) = 2x + 2',
      'g(x) = 2x + 8',
      'g(x) = 2x - 2',
      'g(x) = 4x + 2',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'A',
    explanation: 'Since f(g(x)) = 4(g(x)) - 3, set this equal to 8x + 5: 4(g(x)) - 3 = 8x + 5. Add 3 to both sides: 4(g(x)) = 8x + 8. Divide by 4: g(x) = 2x + 2. Checking, f(g(x)) = 4(2x + 2) - 3 = 8x + 8 - 3 = 8x + 5, which matches. ACT Tip: To find an unknown inner function from a composite function equation, substitute the outer function\'s rule symbolically and solve algebraically for the inner function.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-geo-043',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Geometry',
    difficulty: Difficulty.hard,
    questionText: 'A cone has a radius of 4 cm and a slant height of 11 cm. What is its total surface area, in square centimeters, in terms of pi? (Total surface area = pi r^2 + pi r l, where l is the slant height.)',
    options: [
      '44 pi',
      '60 pi',
      '68 pi',
      '76 pi',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'B',
    explanation: 'Compute the base area: pi r^2 = pi (4)^2 = 16 pi. Compute the lateral area: pi r l = pi (4)(11) = 44 pi. Add the two: 16 pi + 44 pi = 60 pi square centimeters. ACT Tip: A cone\'s total surface area combines its circular base area with its lateral (side) area; compute these two parts separately before adding.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-spd-044',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Statistics and Probability',
    difficulty: Difficulty.hard,
    questionText: 'A survey of 400 people found that the number of books they read per year is normally distributed with a mean of 18 books and a standard deviation of 5 books. Approximately how many people read between 8 and 28 books per year?',
    options: [
      '272',
      '340',
      '380',
      '396',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'C',
    explanation: 'The range 8 to 28 books is exactly two standard deviations below and above the mean of 18 (18 - 2(5) = 8 and 18 + 2(5) = 28). By the empirical rule, approximately 95% of a normal distribution falls within two standard deviations of the mean. Applying this to 400 people: 0.95 x 400 = 380 people. ACT Tip: Recognize when a range matches exactly one, two, or three standard deviations from the mean, then apply the empirical rule percentages of approximately 68%, 95%, and 99.7%, respectively.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-num-045',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Number and Quantity',
    difficulty: Difficulty.hard,
    questionText: 'If i^2 = -1, what is the value of (5 + 2i)(3 - i)?',
    options: [
      '17 + i',
      '13 - 5i',
      '15 - 2i',
      '17 - i',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'A',
    explanation: 'Use the distributive (FOIL) method: (5)(3) + (5)(-i) + (2i)(3) + (2i)(-i) = 15 - 5i + 6i - 2i^2. Combine like terms: 15 + i - 2i^2. Since i^2 = -1, replace -2i^2 with -2(-1) = 2. The result is 15 + 2 + i = 17 + i. ACT Tip: When multiplying complex numbers, remember to replace i^2 with -1 during simplification, since this step often changes the sign of the real part of the result.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-alg-046',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Algebra',
    difficulty: Difficulty.hard,
    questionText: 'Solve for x: log base 2 of (x + 9) = 6.',
    options: [
      '6',
      '55',
      '59',
      '64',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'B',
    explanation: 'The equation log base 2 of (x + 9) = 6 means 2^6 = x + 9. Since 2^6 = 64, this gives 64 = x + 9. Subtract 9 from both sides: x = 55. Checking, log base 2 of (55 + 9) = log base 2 of 64 = 6, since 2^6 = 64, which matches. ACT Tip: Convert a logarithmic equation log base b of (expression) = c into its equivalent exponential form b^c = expression before solving algebraically.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-fun-047',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Functions',
    difficulty: Difficulty.hard,
    questionText: 'The function p(x) = x^3 - 3x^2 - 10x + 24 has a root at x = 2. What are the other two roots?',
    options: [
      'x = 4 and x = -3',
      'x = -4 and x = 3',
      'x = 4 and x = 3',
      'x = -4 and x = -3',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'A',
    explanation: 'Since x = 2 is a root, (x - 2) is a factor. Dividing x^3 - 3x^2 - 10x + 24 by (x - 2) using synthetic division with root 2 gives coefficients 1, -1, -12, with remainder 0, corresponding to the quotient x^2 - x - 12. Factor this quadratic: x^2 - x - 12 = (x - 4)(x + 3), since -4 x 3 = -12 and -4 + 3 = -1, matching. Setting each factor to zero gives x = 4 and x = -3. ACT Tip: After identifying one root of a cubic, use synthetic or polynomial division to reduce it to a quadratic, which can then be factored or solved with the quadratic formula.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-geo-048',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Geometry',
    difficulty: Difficulty.hard,
    questionText: 'A line has the equation 4x - 3y = 18. What is the equation of a line perpendicular to this line that passes through the point (0, 2)?',
    options: [
      'y = (4/3)x + 2',
      'y = -(3/4)x + 2',
      'y = (3/4)x + 2',
      'y = -(4/3)x + 2',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'B',
    explanation: 'Rewrite 4x - 3y = 18 in slope-intercept form: -3y = -4x + 18, so y = (4/3)x - 6. This line has slope 4/3. A perpendicular line has a slope that is the negative reciprocal: -3/4. Using point-slope form with the point (0, 2), which is already the y-intercept, the equation is y = -(3/4)x + 2. ACT Tip: The slope of a line perpendicular to a line with slope m is the negative reciprocal, -1/m; flip the fraction and change its sign.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-spd-049',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Statistics and Probability',
    difficulty: Difficulty.hard,
    questionText: 'A committee of 3 people is to be chosen from a group of 10 people. How many different committees are possible?',
    options: [
      '30',
      '120',
      '720',
      '1000',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'B',
    explanation: 'Since the order of selection does not matter, use the combination formula: C(10,3) = 10! / (3! x 7!) = (10 x 9 x 8) / (3 x 2 x 1) = 720 / 6 = 120. ACT Tip: Use combinations, not permutations, whenever the order of selection does not matter, such as forming a committee or group.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-num-050',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Number and Quantity',
    difficulty: Difficulty.hard,
    questionText: 'What is the sum of the first 12 terms of the arithmetic sequence 6, 11, 16, 21, ...?',
    options: [
      '372',
      '390',
      '402',
      '432',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'C',
    explanation: 'The sequence has first term a1 = 6 and common difference d = 5. The 12th term is a12 = a1 + (12 - 1)d = 6 + 11(5) = 6 + 55 = 61. The sum of the first n terms is S = n(a1 + an)/2 = 12(6 + 61)/2 = 12(67)/2 = 804/2 = 402. ACT Tip: For an arithmetic series, first find the last term using an = a1 + (n-1)d, then apply the sum formula Sn = n(a1 + an)/2 rather than adding every term individually.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-alg-051',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Algebra',
    difficulty: Difficulty.hard,
    questionText: 'If |4x - 7| = 13, what is the sum of all possible values of x?',
    options: [
      '3',
      '3.5',
      '7/2',
      '4',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'C',
    explanation: 'An absolute value equation |4x - 7| = 13 splits into two cases. Case 1: 4x - 7 = 13, so 4x = 20, giving x = 5. Case 2: 4x - 7 = -13, so 4x = -6, giving x = -3/2. The sum of all possible values is 5 + (-3/2) = 10/2 - 3/2 = 7/2. ACT Tip: Always solve both the positive and negative case of an absolute value equation, since skipping the negative case misses a valid solution.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-fun-052',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Functions',
    difficulty: Difficulty.hard,
    questionText: 'For the function f(x) = (x - 5)/(x^2 - 25), which value(s) of x must be excluded from the domain?',
    options: [
      'x = 5 only',
      'x = 5 and x = -5',
      'x = -5 only',
      'x = 25 and x = -25',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'B',
    explanation: 'A rational function is undefined wherever its denominator equals zero. Set the denominator equal to zero: x^2 - 25 = 0, so x^2 = 25, giving x = 5 or x = -5. These values must be excluded from the domain. The numerator being zero at x = 5 does not change this; x = 5 must still be excluded because it also makes the denominator zero, regardless of the numerator\'s value there. ACT Tip: To find domain restrictions for a rational function, set only the denominator equal to zero and solve; even if a numerator root matches, the value is still excluded if the denominator is also zero there.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-geo-053',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Geometry',
    difficulty: Difficulty.hard,
    questionText: 'In triangle ABC, angle A = 50 degrees, side a (opposite angle A) = 11, and side b (opposite angle B) = 13. Using the Law of Sines, what is the measure of angle B, to the nearest degree? (sin 50 degrees is approximately 0.766)',
    options: [
      '58 degrees',
      '60 degrees',
      '65 degrees',
      '73 degrees',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'C',
    explanation: 'The Law of Sines states a/sin(A) = b/sin(B). Substituting known values: 11/sin(50 degrees) = 13/sin(B). Cross-multiply: 11 sin(B) = 13 sin(50 degrees) = 13(0.766) = 9.958. Divide by 11: sin(B) = 0.905. Taking the inverse sine, B is approximately 64.8 degrees, which rounds to 65 degrees. ACT Tip: The Law of Sines applies to any triangle, not just right triangles, whenever you know a side and its opposite angle plus one more piece of information.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-spd-054',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Statistics and Probability',
    difficulty: Difficulty.hard,
    questionText: 'Two events, A and B, are independent. P(A) = 0.5 and P(B) = 0.4. What is P(A or B)?',
    options: [
      '0.6',
      '0.7',
      '0.9',
      '0.2',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'B',
    explanation: 'For any two events, P(A or B) = P(A) + P(B) - P(A and B). Since A and B are independent, P(A and B) = P(A) x P(B) = 0.5 x 0.4 = 0.2. Substituting: P(A or B) = 0.5 + 0.4 - 0.2 = 0.7. ACT Tip: When combining probabilities with "or," subtract the overlap, P(A and B), to avoid double-counting outcomes that satisfy both events.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-num-055',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Number and Quantity',
    difficulty: Difficulty.hard,
    questionText: 'Simplify: the square root of 80 minus the square root of 20, expressed in simplest radical form.',
    options: [
      '2 times the square root of 5',
      '3 times the square root of 5',
      '4 times the square root of 5',
      '5 times the square root of 5',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'A',
    explanation: 'Simplify each radical: the square root of 80 = the square root of (16 x 5) = 4 times the square root of 5, and the square root of 20 = the square root of (4 x 5) = 2 times the square root of 5. Subtracting: 4 times the square root of 5 minus 2 times the square root of 5 equals 2 times the square root of 5. ACT Tip: Before adding or subtracting radicals, simplify each one to its simplest form so that like radical terms can be combined.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-alg-056',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Algebra',
    difficulty: Difficulty.hard,
    questionText: 'A boat travels 96 miles upstream against a current in 8 hours, and the same 96 miles downstream with the current in 6 hours. What is the speed of the current, in miles per hour?',
    options: [
      '1',
      '2',
      '3',
      '4',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'B',
    explanation: 'Let b be the boat\'s speed in still water and c be the current\'s speed. Upstream: b - c = 96/8 = 12. Downstream: b + c = 96/6 = 16. Adding the two equations: 2b = 28, so b = 14. Substituting into b - c = 12: 14 - c = 12, so c = 2 miles per hour. Checking: 14 - 2 = 12 matches the upstream rate, and 14 + 2 = 16 matches the downstream rate. ACT Tip: For upstream and downstream rate problems, set up two equations using speed = distance/time for each direction, then add or subtract the equations to isolate one variable.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-fun-057',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Functions',
    difficulty: Difficulty.hard,
    questionText: 'If sin(theta) = 7/25 and theta is in the first quadrant, what is the value of cos(theta)?',
    options: [
      '7/25',
      '18/25',
      '24/25',
      '25/24',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'C',
    explanation: 'Using the Pythagorean identity sin^2(theta) + cos^2(theta) = 1, substitute sin(theta) = 7/25: (7/25)^2 + cos^2(theta) = 1, so 49/625 + cos^2(theta) = 1. Subtract 49/625 from both sides: cos^2(theta) = 576/625. Taking the square root: cos(theta) = 24/25 (positive, since theta is in the first quadrant where cosine is positive). ACT Tip: Use the Pythagorean identity sin^2(theta) + cos^2(theta) = 1 to find one trig ratio from another, and use the given quadrant to determine the correct sign.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-geo-058',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Geometry',
    difficulty: Difficulty.hard,
    questionText: 'A circle is centered at (3, -6) and has a radius of 8. What is the equation of the circle?',
    options: [
      '(x - 3)^2 + (y + 6)^2 = 64',
      '(x + 3)^2 + (y - 6)^2 = 64',
      '(x - 3)^2 + (y + 6)^2 = 8',
      '(x - 3)^2 + (y - 6)^2 = 64',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'A',
    explanation: 'The standard equation of a circle is (x - h)^2 + (y - k)^2 = r^2, where (h, k) is the center and r is the radius. With center (3, -6), h = 3 and k = -6, so the equation includes (x - 3)^2 and (y - (-6))^2 = (y + 6)^2. The radius squared is 8^2 = 64. The full equation is (x - 3)^2 + (y + 6)^2 = 64. ACT Tip: Be careful with the sign inside each squared term of a circle\'s equation; a negative center coordinate produces a plus sign inside the parentheses, due to the subtraction in the standard form.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-spd-059',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Statistics and Probability',
    difficulty: Difficulty.hard,
    questionText: 'A data set of 20 values has a standard deviation of 6. If every value in the data set is multiplied by 5, what is the new standard deviation?',
    options: [
      '6',
      '11',
      '30',
      '150',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'C',
    explanation: 'When every value in a data set is multiplied by a constant k, the standard deviation is also multiplied by that same constant. Multiplying the original standard deviation of 6 by 5 gives a new standard deviation of 30. ACT Tip: Multiplying a data set by a constant scales the standard deviation by that same constant, while adding a constant to every value does not change the standard deviation at all.',
  ),
  ActQuestion(
    id: 's03-math-num-060',
    setNumber: 3,
    section: ActSection.math,
    skillArea: 'Number and Quantity',
    difficulty: Difficulty.hard,
    questionText: 'If x and y are positive integers such that 2^x x 3^y = 432, what is the value of x + y?',
    options: [
      '6',
      '7',
      '8',
      '9',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'B',
    explanation: 'Find the prime factorization of 432: 432 = 16 x 27 = 2^4 x 3^3. Comparing to 2^x x 3^y, this gives x = 4 and y = 3. Therefore x + y = 4 + 3 = 7. ACT Tip: To match an expression like a^x x b^y to a given number, find that number\'s full prime factorization and compare the exponents of matching prime bases directly.',
  ),
