      'She has abandoned research on canvassing entirely in favor of studying social media interventions',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'B',
    explanation: 'The passage explicitly states Nandakumar "remains cautiously confident that canvassing retains a meaningful, if likely somewhat diminished, advantage over impersonal contact methods," while also acknowledging the effect is "considerably more context-dependent" than early accounts suggested, precisely matching this nuanced characterization. The passage does not state Nandakumar believes canvassing has no effect at all; she explicitly maintains it retains a meaningful advantage, just one that is more variable than once believed. The passage explicitly describes her acknowledging a likely "somewhat diminished" effect compared to the original study, directly contradicting a claim that she believes the effect is completely unchanged. Social media interventions are never mentioned anywhere in the passage as a subject of Nandakumar\'s research. ACT Tip: When a passage describes an expert\'s nuanced, qualified position, look for language explicitly balancing confidence with acknowledged uncertainty, rather than selecting an answer that overstates the position in either direction.',
