    questionText: 'Based on the passage, which of the following best explains the apparent tension critics have identified between Esperanto\'s design and its stated goal of neutrality?',
    options: [
      'Esperanto\'s grammar contains too many irregular verbs, making it difficult for any learner to master',
      'Esperanto\'s vocabulary and grammar draw primarily from European language roots, which may have limited its appeal as a genuinely neutral choice for non-European speakers',
